   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# ✂️ One Image → Whole Asset Pack — Geekatplay GameAssetMake\n### (c) Geekatplay Studio / Vladimir Chopine — geekatplay.com\n\nLoad **one environment image** (a concept painting, a screenshot, AI render) and this\nworkflow extracts every distinct object in it — buildings, benches, lamps, crates —\nas **individual 3D game assets**, delivered straight into the engine at positions that\nmirror the picture. **No diffusion models needed**: this workflow runs without any\ncheckpoint installed.\n\n## The pipeline\n1. **Load Image** — pick the scene image to mine for assets.\n2. **✂️ Scene Element Extractor** — finds the objects, cuts each onto a clean white\n   square (the framing image-to-3D APIs require), and writes the asset manifest.\n3. **🖼️ Gallery** — the run PAUSES; untick anything you don't want, then *Approve & Continue*.\n4. **🧊 3D Generator** — each approved crop becomes a mesh (Tripo / Meshy / HiTem3D).\n5. **📐 Placement Manager → ⚡ Engine Bridge** — true-scale import, placed like the picture.\n\n## ✂️ Extractor properties\n- **max_assets** — cap on extracted objects (default 12).\n- **min_object_area_pct** — detections smaller than this % of the image are noise; raise it\n  if you get clutter, lower it to catch small props (default 0.5%).\n- **crop_padding_pct** — margin added around each detection so nothing is clipped (8%).\n- **output_size** — white-canvas size per object; 1024 suits every 3D provider.\n- **matte_on_white** — GrabCut cutout onto pure white (needs `opencv-python`; without it\n  the raw crop is used and busy backgrounds may leak into the mesh).\n- **detection** — `vlm+heuristic` (default): a local Ollama **vision** model (gemma3:12b)\n  finds and NAMES objects, falling back to free local blob analysis when Ollama is off.\n  Photographs and busy scenes really want the VLM; simple renders work with `heuristic`.\n- **art_style** — written into each asset's prompt so later regenerations keep the look.\n- **scene_span_m** — how wide (meters) the pictured area really is. Object positions in\n  the image map to world positions through this, so the pack re-assembles like the picture.\n\n## Before you run\n- **Ollama** (optional, recommended): `ollama pull gemma3:12b` — better detection + names.\n- **API keys**: type once into the 3D Generator with *remember_keys* ON → saved to the\n  OS credential vault, never into this JSON.\n- **dry_run_mock is ON** by default — flip to *Live Cloud APIs* to spend credits.\n- **Engine bridge** running (Unreal :30010 / Unity :8080) — the 🔌 check node shows status.\n"
   ],
   "title": "✂️ READ ME — One Image → Asset Pack",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
